  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bfa36fdea331abe4cb2b293833ff63a0, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 188400156672
    m_Localized: "Alter-Echoes are your main source of income while away. At the
      end of each run each resource you earned calculates its income per minute and
      stores your lifetime best. Alter Echoes use this value to generate resources.\n\nEcho
      Power is a value that determines the percentage of resources you receive. It
      is visible at the top right of the Alter Echoes screen.\n \nResources will
      be gathered and brought to eva for storage. When you return she will happily
      give them to you, all you have to do is ask!\nThese will generate whether the
      game is open or closed!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 478381752320
    m_Localized: 'Buffs are short-term, timed powers that expire when they run out
      or if you return to town.  They can be autocast after completing the required
      quest for the slot and the aucocasting defaults to on. You can toggle it off
      by clicking the slot in the buffs management window.


      Buff cooldowns
      can be reduced via Eva''s Cauldron.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 492340396032
    m_Localized: 'Caleb will enter combat automatically, and only engage enemies
      who get in the way! Tasks first fun later.


      Reaching your 10th, 100th,
      1,000th, and 10,000th kill against a specific enemy will grant you 25% bonus
      damage against that specific enemy.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 512217202688
    m_Localized: "Echoes are alternate versions of Caleb who will shift slightly
      into his reality to help out under various circumstances.\n\nEach echo can
      have a combination of Calebs skillset. But most Echoes won't have them all.\n\nThe
      main difference in Echo behaviour comes from whether or not they are combat
      enabled.\nCombat enabled Echoes have two different styles depending on whether
      or not they can also complete tasks. \n\nA combat enabled Echo that does NOT
      have the ability to do tasks will seek out enemies specifically.\nA combat
      enabled Echo that DOES have the ability to do tasks will prioritize tasks over
      combat and only engage enemies that see them.\n\nEchoes that do not have combat
      will not be targetted by or target enemies.\n\nDev Note | Right now there are
      no echoes in the game that can do both combat and tasks. Echoes from Milestones
      specifically seek out tasks for that skills milestone EG an echo spawned with
      woodcutting will only seek out woodcutting tasks."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 532437942272
    m_Localized: 'For each kill you get on a run your resource bonus goes up by 2%
      During combat this is temporarily set back to 0%


      Aim to retreat just
      before combat gets too tough for you to handle so that you get as many bonus
      resources as possible!'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 698595295232
    m_Localized: 'Tasks are the primary purpose of Caleb''s journey. Gathering resources
      for the town is essential to growth.


      These are completed automatically,
      and you will complete them faster as your skills level.


      Task spawns
      have a range from minimum to maximum distance, however after reaching maximum
      distance their chance to spawn goes down by 90% With this considered once all
      tasks are at their maximum the weight system will average out and all tasks
      will be equally available based on their weights.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 505754247643136
    m_Localized: 'Quests have different types of conditions that need to be met before
      you hand them in.


      <b>Information</b> | These quests are instantly completed,
      either for story, or to guide you through the intro.

      <b>Gathering</b>
      | Thse quests require you to gather resources and hand them in to complete.

      <b>Kills</b>
      | Kill enemies and report back to complete these.

      <b>Meet</b> | Require
      you to meet a certain NPC most of whom are found at specific distances reached.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3785742338113536
    m_Localized: "Upon reaching certain distances from the town Carl will reap your
      soul ensuring you don't stray too far. \nYou can view your maximum reaping
      distance in the statistics under the General Tab.\n\nReaping distance is increased
      via the following methods.\n<b>Being Reaped</b> | Increases distance by 1%
      of your current maximum reaping distance.\n<b>Quests</b> | Some quests will
      provide a reaping distance increase."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6939642239008768
    m_Localized: v1.2.6
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7986628786536448
    m_Localized: 'Dragon slaying pope

      Invariel

      tanty.

      Mellifas

      Latimer
      Cross

      MatHeadGetz

      appleguy

      AwesomePhoenix

      boiledpotato

      eli

      GLUTTONY

      Gudu

      Mentocado

      Nuclearion

      Quackers

      Rugmuk

      SaintPlays

      SCHMUGGLER

      WaringMcMarrin'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9824133160779776
    m_Localized: "Ivan's forge is a magical place. Whether you're chilling in town
      or out on the road, you can help guide him as he improves his smithing skills.\n\nThis
      is where you craft gear and choose the best stats for your build. \nRight now
      there are 7 stats that can be rolled on gear with each piece guaranteeing a
      specific one.\n\n<sprite=198> = Damage.\n<sprite=200> = Attack Speed.\n<sprite=199>
      = Crit Chance.  \n\n<sprite=202> = Health.\n<sprite=203> = Regen.\n<sprite=201>
      = Defense.\n<sprite=204> = Movement.\n\n<sprite=192> = Upgrade.\n<sprite=193>
      = Downgrade. \n<sprite=194> = No change.\n<sprite=195> Stat is not on new item.\n<sprite=196>
      Stat is not on old item.\n\n<b>Weapon</b> | Guarantees <sprite=198>\n<b>Helmet</b>
      | Guarantees <sprite=202>\n<b>Chest</b> | Guarantees <sprite=201>\n<b>Boots</b>
      | Guarantees <sprite=204> which is exclusive to this slot.\n\nGear is automatically
      salvaged when you craft a new piece, select a different slot, or close the
      game.\n\nDepending on rarity you can receive up to 5 stats on a piece of gear.
      There are plans to add additional stats to gear in the future!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9824133185945600
    m_Localized: "Hey guys Dev here. \n\nIf you want your names in the enemy name
      random pool of names then please jump into discord and ask in the EoV Chat
      :)\n\nThe plan now is to spend a few days updating existing content, quality
      of life. Polish, and additional content for those systems. Would love your
      input on discord!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9898115700506624
    m_Localized: "\u2022 Feathers have been removed from trees and added to chickens.
      The Vast One apologizes for the error in creation.\n\u2022 Reap distance no
      longer has a formatted number, much easier to see the exact number at higher
      values now.\n\u2022 Improved the wording on buff quest rewards.\n\u2022 Button
      sounds.\n\u2022 You can now import/export your saves.\n1.2.5\n\u2022 Chickens!\n\u2022
      I forgot to mention, cauldron is now locked behind some buff quests.\n\u2022
      If you have save migration issues, switch to the unstable branch on steam to
      import your old save.\n\u2022 Extended the Cauldron window to be 6 slots wide.\n\u2022
      Animations now speed up with task speed!\n\u2022 Added the next 5 tiers of
      Resource Tiers.\n\u2022 Crafted items have no bonus, are set to max tier background
      and listed as \"Crafted\" in the items panel.\n\u2022 Fixed a bug where dice
      wasn't working properly.\n1.2.4\n\u2022 13 New Achievements.\n\u2022 34 New
      Quests.\n\u2022 New Tiers for resources, low chance to tier up every time they're
      collected naturally.\n\u2022 Updated the Quest window to be more clear.\n\u2022
      Echoes no longer expire while on task, instead they wait till their task is
      complete and then expire.\n\u2022 Echo bars now show as Green till 50% health,
      Yellow till 10%, and Red till they expire.\n\u2022 A Matter of Health, and
      Tracking Twins now award: 0.5% Increased Alter-Echo power. These are not retroactively
      granted, you will require a new save if you want these rewards and have completed
      the quest.\n\u2022 The Resource Doubler buff is now a Resource Multiplier buff
      so that it can scale with quests!\n\u2022 Added indicators to the pie charts
      to show that you can hover over them or tap on mobile.\n\u2022 Major FPS performance
      improvements across the whole UI.\n\u2022 The farmlands no longer have enemies
      or increase your reap distance when being reaped.\n\u2022 Removed local avoidance
      from Caleb, echoes can now pass through him.\n\u2022 The Vast One has given
      Carl the secrets to defense, he can now bypass enemies defense to reap them
      correctly for you.\n\u2022 Vampirism has been changed. We no longer have lifesteal,
      instead its a percent regen buff. It has been renamed accordingly.\n\u2022
      Buffs now have their cooldowns cleared when a run is longer than their cooldown.\n\u2022
      The Cauldron now only accepts food items.\n\u2022 The Cauldron now shows all
      available slots instead of only 6.\n\u2022 0 Count items are no longer selectable
      in the Cauldron.\n\u2022 Removed Onion.\n\u2022 Added collection completeion
      bonus to AE categories buffs the Echo Power in the AE screen.\n\u2022 Adjusted
      the overall curve of stat distribution on gear. It will now be much harder
      to roll perfect Vastium gear. And we should see less of a jump in stats on
      the earlier gear.\n\u2022 The forge now shows the tier of gear that you have
      equipped and roll.\n\u2022 You can now upgrade cores in the forge.\n\u2022
      Forge Stats now shows a Quality section which works properly unlike the old
      score system which was comparing your best upgrade rather than the best it
      could be.\n\u2022 The bonus damage from the dice now just shows on the value
      itself, removed (+{bonusValue}) from the end.\n\u2022 Fixed an issue causing
      multiple save events to trigger in a single frame during AE collection.\n\u2022
      New enemy balance standard damage scaling for Skelly Mage and Large Slimes
      5 damage per level.\n\u2022 New enemy balance standard damage scaling for Skelly
      Archer and Medium Slimes 2.5 damage per level.\n\u2022 New enemy balance standard
      damage scaling for Skelly Swordsman and Small Slimes 1 damage per level.\n\u2022
      Removed migration systems."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 12027031164698624
    m_Localized: "The Cauldron is Evas connection to the Vast One.\n\nTossing ingredients
      in summons the power of The Vast One. Pulling in your entire stockpile of that
      resource! It does however require at least two types of resources, for flavour
      reasons.\nOnce you toss ingredients in you will recieve a number of stew based
      on the rarity and count of the resources tossed in. After which you can taste
      the stew to draw from the well of the Vast One's power. You will receive cards
      based on Eva's level which affects her weights as displayed on the Cauldron
      screen.\n\nEach card has a tier from 1-8 and levels up at the following thresholds.
      For now there are no additional bonuses for collecting beyond the cap of that
      tier but you can continue for as long as you like. Perhaps more power will
      come from this in the future? The following thresholds are currently implemented.\n\nEach
      category except for the buff category will additionally tier up as you pass
      the threshold with all cards in it. If all cards are Tier 2 or higher then
      the category will be Tier 2. Each Tier you complete in this fashion will award
      0.1% Alter Echo Power.\n\nResource Tiers\n\u2022 1 | Alter Echo Power for this
      cards resource +10%\n\u2022 25 | 10%<sprite=194>25%\n\u2022 75 | 25%<sprite=194>50%\n\u2022
      200 | 50%<sprite=194>75%\n\u2022 750 | 75%<sprite=194>120%\n\u2022 1500 | 120%<sprite=194>180%\n\u2022
      3500 | 180%<sprite=194>250%\n\u2022 10000 | 250%<sprite=194>400%\nBuff Tiers\n\u2022
      1 | Cooldown -5%, Buff Power: 0%\n\u2022 5 | Cooldown -10%, Buff Power: 0%\n\u2022
      25 | Cooldown -15%, Buff Power: 5%\n\u2022 75 | Cooldown -25%, Buff Power:
      10%\n\u2022 200 | Cooldown -40%, Buff Power: 15%\n\u2022 750 | Cooldown -60%,
      Buff Power: 20%\n\u2022 1500 | Cooldown -80%, Buff Power: 25%\n\u2022 3000
      | Cooldown -100%, Buff Power: 30%"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
